comment.body:
I think we can avoid maintaining the live files set, as well as updating it on every `updateCommit` call.

We can pass a `Supplier<Set<String>>` to the `maybeScheduleObsoleteRegionsEviction`  and `submitObsoleteRegionsEviction` methods, and later when the runnable submitted to `cacheService.submitAsyncEviction()` is executed it calls the supplier.

The initial supplier could be something like:
```java
Set<String> localFiles() {
      try (var ignored = readLock.acquire()) {
          return Set.copyOf(localFiles.keySet());
      }
  }
```

